<bold>Publisher's note:</bold> Springer Nature remains neutral with regard to jurisdictional claims in published maps and institutional affiliations.</p></fn></fn-group><ack><title>Acknowledgements</title><p>The authors thank A. Dizeux for his help in the figures design and A. Rogers for English revision. This work was supported by the European Research Council under the European Union&#x02019;s Seventh Framework Programme (FP7/2007-2013)/ERC Advanced grant agreement n&#x000b0; 339244-FUSIMAGINE).</p></ack><notes notes-type="author-contribution"><title>Author Contributions</title><p>M.I., D.C., J.-L.G., L.C. and M.T. conceived and designed the study together. D.C. and L.C. collected the data as neurosurgeons. M.I. and J.-L.G. collected the data as physicists. M.I. and L.C. performed the data analysis. M.I. and D.C. wrote the manuscript. All authors reviewed the manuscript.</p></notes><notes notes-type="COI-statement"><sec id="FPar1"><title>Competing Interests</title><p id="Par35">The authors declare that they have no competing interests.</p></sec></notes><ref-list id="Bib1"><title>References</title><ref id="CR1"><label>1.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ebeling</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmid</surname><given-names>UD</given-names></name><name><surname>Reulen</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tumour-surgery within the central motor strip: Surgical results with the aid of electrical motor cortex stimulation</article-title><source>Acta Neurochir. (Wien)</source><year>1989</year><volume>101</volume><fpage>100</fpage><lpage>107</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/BF01410522</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2618812</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR2"><label>2.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grienberger</surname><given-names>C</giv